  "synonym_discrimination": null,
  "usage_note": "**Anyone** and **anybody** mean the same thing and can normally replace each other; **anyone** is more common in writing. **Any one** (written as two words) points to a single one chosen from a group, whether a person, a thing, or an option: *any one of these books*, *any one of the three days*, a different expression from **anyone**.",
